Title: Build the bounded version-0 reverify sweep
Created: 2026-09-02
Author: codex

--- log ---
2026-09-02T15:59Z codex created

--- body ---
## Context

X6 fired on 2026-09-02 through Zotero's installed full-text control plugin. A
real local re-extraction changed a previously nonzero full-text census value to
0 while the attachment item version remained 0; a group-library attachment
remained 0. The md5-widened signal therefore cannot observe later local
re-extractions inside the version-0 class. The ruling commits a bounded idle
re-verify sweep and requires its horizon to be reported.

Evidence: `bench/results/0025-x6-version-dynamics/x6-live-reextract-2026-09-02.json`.

## Actions

1. Walk version-0 attachments in a persistent, fair order during idle time.
2. Re-read and hash a bounded amount per tick; unchanged content stops there,
   changed content re-enters the derivation chain.
3. Persist the cursor so restarts do not repeatedly verify the prefix.
4. Report population, last completed visit, current cursor and worst-case
   horizon through status.
5. Compose with the content-presence probe: one walk performs both checks rather
   than maintaining two independent scans.

## Test

- ManualClock proves the per-tick bound and a full fair cycle.
- Restart mid-cycle and prove the cursor resumes.
- A same-version changed body is re-derived; an unchanged body is not.
- A missing cache becomes the ruled cache-lost state rather than deletion.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Work per tick is bounded and the horizon is derived and reported.
- [ ] Every version-0 attachment is revisited fairly across restarts.
- [ ] Same-version content change reaches re-derivation.
- [ ] The content-presence probe shares the walk.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check` pass.
